    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1426">

                <pb facs="0938" n="822" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg822"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/335.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-21T23:00:00-07:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 21, 1914, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Villa’s decree permitting Spaniards to return to Torreon and Chihuahua
                    will be published in newspapers to-morrow provided for return of all who are
                    conscious of not having taken part in any manner in internal affairs of Mexico.
                    Am forwarding copy of text by mail. This has had good effect and many will
                    return.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">G. C. Carothers</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
